{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-35558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $W$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree $5$ or greater. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-35558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **$W$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, the zero polynomial has degree $0$, which is less than $5.$\n\nOn the other hand: \n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $5$ (or greater), the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ has the same degree. $\\,✓$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-35558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0bf776a02d5a82f416dd58be6d8cd8f79656be51b653125fe6b8ce528953f4c4"} {"question" "q-35558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-35558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$W$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x)\\in W$"] ["text" "$W$ does not contain the zero element"] ["text" "addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials do not satisfy the distributive laws"] ["text" "addition of polynomials is not associative"] ["text" "addition of polynomials is not commutative"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-35558" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$W$ does not contain the zero element"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $Y$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree exactly $2.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed.** *\n\nIndeed, let's consider, for example, the polynomials $p(x)={x}^{2}+x$ and $q(x)=-{x}^{2}.$ Then $p,q\\in Y,$ but \n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)={x}^{2}+x+(-{x}^{2})=x\\notin Y\n$$\n\n because $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p+q)=1\\ne 2.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- $1\\cdot p=p$ for all $p\\in Y.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0bf776a02d5a82f416dd58be6d8cd8f79656be51b653125fe6b8ce528953f4c4"} {"question" "q-106929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$1\\cdot p\\ne p$ for some $p\\in Y$"] ["text" "addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials do not satisfy the distributive laws"] ["text" "addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed"] ["text" "addition of polynomials is not associative"] ["text" "addition of polynomials is not commutative"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106929" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$F$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, evaluating the zero function $f(x)=0$ at $x=0,$ we have $f(0)=0\\ne \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in F.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of functions satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0bf776a02d5a82f416dd58be6d8cd8f79656be51b653125fe6b8ce528953f4c4"} {"question" "q-106813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in F$"] ["text" "$F$ does not contain the zero element"] ["text" "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $F$ do not satisfy the distributive laws"] ["text" "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not associative"] ["text" "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not commutative"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106813" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$F$ does not contain the zero element"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106933" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $I$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)={2}^{ax},$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106933" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$I$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, $f(x)={2}^{ax}>0$ for all $x\\in R$ for any $a\\in R,$ hence the zero function $z(x)=0\\notin I.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in I.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is commutative. $\\,✓$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106933" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0bf776a02d5a82f416dd58be6d8cd8f79656be51b653125fe6b8ce528953f4c4"} {"question" "q-106933" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106933" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in I$"] ["text" "$I$ does not contain the zero element"] ["text" "addition and scalar multiplication of functions do not satisfy the distributive laws"] ["text" "addition of functions is not associative"] ["text" "addition of functions is not commutative"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106933" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$I$ does not contain the zero element"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-94809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $J$ be the set of purely imaginary complex numbers, that is, complex numbers of the form  $ai,$ where  $a$ is a nonzero real number. Complete the following sentence: \n\n*$J$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of complex numbers and scalar multiplication of a complex number by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-94809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$J$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of complex numbers and scalar multiplication of a complex number by a real number) because **multiplication of $z\\in J$ by real scalars is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =0$ and $z=i,$ then $\\alpha \\cdot z=0\\cdot i=0\\notin J.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $J$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition  in $J$ is commutative.  $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $J$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- If  $z\\in J$ then $z=ai$ for some $a\\in R.$ Hence, $-z=(-a)i\\in J$   since $-a\\in R.$ $\\,✓$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-94809" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0bf776a02d5a82f416dd58be6d8cd8f79656be51b653125fe6b8ce528953f4c4"} {"question" "q-94809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-94809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$J$ does not contain the element $-z$ for every $z\\in J$"] ["text" "Addition and scalar multiplication in $J$ satisfy the distributive laws"] ["text" "addition  in $J$ is commutative"] ["text" "addition in $J$ is associative"] ["text" "multiplication of $z\\in J$ by real  scalars is not closed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-94809" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "multiplication of $z\\in J$ by real  scalars is not closed"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $y$ is a vector such that $x+y=0$, then $y=-x.$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0bf776a02d5a82f416dd58be6d8cd8f79656be51b653125fe6b8ce528953f4c4"} {"question" "q-106938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A4}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A4}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A1}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*$0\\cdot 0=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A7}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A5}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A7}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0bf776a02d5a82f416dd58be6d8cd8f79656be51b653125fe6b8ce528953f4c4"} {"question" "q-106944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A7}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A6}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A6}$, $\\text{A3}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A5}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-106944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-74671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $x$ is a vector such that $-x+w=w$ for some $w\\in V$, then $x=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axioms  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-74671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-74671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/140