x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-35661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add }(-w)\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-35661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0bf776a02d5a82f416dd58be6d8cd8f79656be51b653125fe6b8ce528953f4c4"} {"question" "q-35661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-35661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A7}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A4}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A3}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "q-35661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/state.json" "file_sha256" "eeef507c4542ce6c5158d41e63602c5e3630373140514877b9a4a2290ab6c228"} {"question" "e-8224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V$ be the set of all real polynomials of degree exactly $3$, equipped with the usual addition and scalar multiplication operations. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space because $\\textrm{_________}\\,.$*\n\n- the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$\n\n- $V$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x) \\in V$\n\n- addition of polynomials is not commutative" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/example-8224.json" "file_sha256" "191138051192cef3170327a8e5c8e92b501668e7db541297e09da4e4a9323998"} {"question" "e-8224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer  is as follows:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space because **the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$.** *\n\nFor instance, if $p(x) = 1 +x^3$ and $q(x) = 1-x^3$, then $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are in $V.$ However  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x)+q(x) & =(1+{x}^{3})+(1-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2\\notin V.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative.\n\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $3$, the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ also has degree $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/example-8224.json" "file_sha256" "191138051192cef3170327a8e5c8e92b501668e7db541297e09da4e4a9323998"} {"question" "e-4792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\textrm A1] - [\\textrm A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $\\mathbf{w}$ is a vector such that $\\mathbf{w}+\\mathbf{w} = \\mathbf{w}$, then $\\mathbf{w}=\\mathbf{0}.$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/example-4792.json" "file_sha256" "c37b10bf22b63b19c7c7e76717c28c97c11612a1e8c78c1ee1f6b1cc14e6ae43"} {"question" "e-4792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the axioms of a vector space, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A2}}[/math]}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A3}}[/math]}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/example-4792.json" "file_sha256" "c37b10bf22b63b19c7c7e76717c28c97c11612a1e8c78c1ee1f6b1cc14e6ae43"} {"question" "q-35583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\text{A8}$, $\\text{A3}$"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "c77032684a890357413062b488003fa7d4eedeff074d3c180069b2f044e1f24c" "reviewer_session" "01a118cc-89a0-7c90-9221-d6599ae13bca" "rationale" "The first blank distributes scalar multiplication over vector addition: α(0+0)=α0+α0, exactly A8. The second removes the additive identity: α0+0=α0, exactly A3. Thus the required top-to-bottom sequence is A8, A3, original option 0. The stored answer has identical labels and order. This is a source-backed derived judgment from the displayed axioms and authentic worked solution. The Incorrect grade concerns the submitted A6, A4 pair, not this reviewed answer." "bindings" {"problem" "3886fd019a8166c8c9641e7fa22ea4009d07f6f9c8b8a43ae88a937e642677a7" "worked_solution" "de970dccbfc8d9bfe34f8955d3d587021a72ba2ff5afefb23477173ac6f27ee1" "original_field" "6311c2692ecc9e906b3d386f13d4f939acaec81c4bc859044be50fd0c59902c8" "reviewed_field" "7c0a2a1e4c4115182e96363b5ea716aa437bb400fda0197598251a629da1d38e" "raw_widget" "48a6a27a3124763cd834b8fe696385ab48652553a3fe5f1ad280d56ad8a5fd24"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-35583-before.png" "sha256" "87017b529fe2611d916e597edbc6cdbce3528db50babf6d3dde276ed2a736596"} {"path" "history-q-35583.png" "sha256" "ef2c8168db652af95d49e9d488204ecf24e74f45e2c2529015cac9a004f4ce8c"} {"path" "q-35583-after.json" "sha256" "3a48cedf26290da536a04c54e3e0dd3031f8959f3c286ab68f91343c985e99d8"}]} {"question" "q-35583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\text{A6}$, $\\text{A3}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A6}$, $\\text{A4}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A3}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A8}$, $\\text{A3}$"] ["text" "$\\text{A8}$, $\\text{A4}$"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044859/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "c77032684a890357413062b488003fa7d4eedeff074d3c180069b2f044e1f24c" "rationale" "The first blank distributes scalar multiplication over vector addition: α(0+0)=α0+α0, exactly A8. The second removes the additive identity: α0+0=α0, exactly A3. Thus the required top-to-bottom sequence is A8, A3, original option 0. The stored answer has identical labels and order. This is a source-backed derived judgment from the displayed axioms and authentic worked solution. The Incorrect grade concerns the submitted A6, A4 pair, not this reviewed answer."}] "usage" {"q-35583" [] "e-4792" [] "e-8224" [] "q-35558" []} "basis" 1791 "retractions" [[17592186184703 :question/problem "Let $W$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x ∈ R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree $5$ or greater. Complete the following sentence:\n\n> *$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $_________$.*"] [17592186184704 :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[A1] - [A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n> *$α0 = 0$ for any $α ∈ R$*\n\n*Proof:*\n$\\begin{bmatrix}α0|= α0 & [given] \\\\ α0|= α(0 + 0) & [axiom A3] \\\\ α0|= α0 + α0 & [axiom __] \\\\ α0 + (- α0)|= (α0 + α0) + (- α0) & [add- α0to both sides] \\\\ α0 + (- α0)|= α0 + (α0 + (- α0)) & [axiom A2] \\\\ 0|= α0 + 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ 0|= α0 & [axiom __]\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe axioms:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}[A1]: x + y = y + x & [A5]: 1 \\cdot x = x \\\\ [A2]: (x + y) + z = x + (y + z) & [A6]: α(βx) = (αβ)x \\\\ [A3]: x + 0 = x & [A7]: (α + β)x = αx + βx \\\\ [A4]: x + (-x) = 0 & [A8]: α(x + y) = αx + αy\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186184704 :question/answer-fields 17592186183113] [17592186184038 :question/problem "Let $V$ be the set of all real polynomials of degree exactly $3$, equipped with the usual addition and scalar multiplication operations. Complete the following sentence:\n\n> *$V$ is **not** a vector space because $\\textrm{_________}\\,$.*\n\n1. the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$\n2. $V$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x) \\in V$\n3. addition of polynomials is not commutative"] [17592186184038 :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n> *$V$ is **not** a vector space because **the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$.***\n\nFor instance, if\n\n$$\np(x) = 1 +x^3\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nq(x) = 1-x^3\n$$\n\n, then $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are in $V$. However\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np(x) + q(x) &= (1 + x^{3}) + (1 - x^{3}) \\\\\n&= 2 ∉ V\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative.\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $3$, the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ also has degree $3$."] [17592186184009 :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\textrm A1] - [\\textrm A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n> *If $\\mathbf{w}$ is a vector such that $\\mathbf{w}+\\mathbf{w} = \\mathbf{w}$, then $\\mathbf{w}=\\mathbf{0}$.*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}w + w|= w & [given] \\\\ (w + w) + (-w)|= w + (-w) & [add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides] \\\\ w + (w + (-w))|= w + (-w) & [axiom __] \\\\ w + 0|= 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ w|= 0 & [axiom __]\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe axioms:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}[A1]: x + y = y + x & [A5]: 1 \\cdot x = x \\\\ [A2]: (x + y) + z = x + (y + z) & [A6]: α(βx) = (αβ)x \\\\ [A3]: x + 0 = x & [A7]: (α + β)x = αx + βx \\\\ [A4]: x + (-x) = 0 & [A8]: α(x + y) = αx + αy\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186184009 :question/worked-solution "Using the axioms of a vector space, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}w + w &= w & [given] \\\\ (w + w) + (-w)|= w + (-w) & [add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides] \\\\ w + (w + (-w))|= w + (-w) & [axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A2}}[/math]] \\\\ w + 0|= 0 & [axiom A4] \\\\ w|= 0 & [axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A3}}[/math]]\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186183108 17592186183109 17592186183110 17592186183111 17592186183112 17592186183114 17592186183115 17592186183116 17592186183117 17592186183118] "immutable_fields" [[17592186183107 :answer-field/correct] [17592186183107 :answer-field/id] [17592186183107 :answer-field/key] [17592186183107 :answer-field/type] [17592186183113 :answer-field/correct] [17592186183113 :answer-field/id] [17592186183113 :answer-field/key] [17592186183113 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
